{"Email normalization is incomplete: blacklist comparison uses toLowerCase() on env values but compares against raw guest string, and existing attendee check is case-sensitive allowing duplicate entries with different casing": 0.9481030106544495, "Authorization logic uses AND (&&) instead of OR (||), requiring a user to be both a team admin AND team owner simultaneously, incorrectly denying access to legitimate team admins who are not owners": 0.9706612825393677, "Validation schema is duplicated in client with uniqueness check but server-side schema lacks this uniqueness validation, creating inconsistency where server may accept duplicate emails if client validation is bypassed": 0.8668530583381653, "Using createMany without transaction protection creates a race condition risk where concurrent requests adding the same guest can fail mid-operation, leaving database and calendar/email state inconsistent": 0.5670714974403381, "Email errors are silently swallowed with a generic console.log, losing the actual error object, stack trace, and context like bookingId/userId, making production debugging difficult": 0.9829905033111572, "getUsersCredentials(ctx.user) retrieves credentials for the logged-in user instead of the booking organizer, causing calendar updates to fail or update the wrong calendar when a non-organizer invokes the mutation": 0.9673041701316833}